## Fee Clarification: Exit Load
### Reusable Support Snippet

  • Exit load is a charge levied only when units are redeemed before the fund’s specified exit‑load period, not on every transaction.
  • The applicable percentage is defined in the scheme’s offer document and can differ between funds; it is not a uniform rate for all mutual funds.
  • The load is imposed by the asset management company as disclosed in the scheme’s terms, not by the distribution platform, and the amount is shown in the redemption statement.
  • If the redemption occurs after the mandatory holding period (or after the exit‑load period specified for the scheme), no exit load is charged.
  • For systematic investment plans, each instalment starts

